## 2. Architecture

### Three-layer model

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  📦 mfaw repo (pip-installable, git-versioned)                     │
│                                                                     │
│   src/mfaw/             content/             schema/                │
│     cli.py                skills/              skill.schema.json    │
│     commands/             agents/              manifest.schema.json │
│     adapters/             rules/               state.schema.json    │
│       base.py             commands/                                 │
│       claude.py           manifest.json                             │
│       cursor.py           adapters/{claude,cursor}/                 │
└──────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
       │  pip install mfaw
       ▼
   $ mfaw <init|sync|publish|nuke|doctor|status|list|use>
       │
       │  resolves: global ⊕ project → effective set
       │  projects: effective set → adapter targets
       ▼
┌─────────────────────────┐    ┌─────────────────────────┐
│  ~/.claude/             │    │  ~/.cursor/             │
│   skills/    (stubs)    │    │   rules/*.mdc           │
│   commands/  (stubs)    │    │                         │
│   settings.json         │    │                         │
│    hooks._mfaw_managed  │    │                         │
└─────────────────────────┘    └─────────────────────────┘
       ▲
       │  ledgers track every mutation
       ▼
   ~/.mfaw/state.json          (global ledger)
   <repo>/.mfaw/state.json     (project ledger)
   ~/.mfaw/projects/index.json (project switcher state)
```

### Three concepts working together

1. **Source of truth** — markdown content in git.
2. **Indirection** — symlinks (preferred) / junctions (Windows dirs) / copy+sentinel (Windows files).
3. **Ledgers** — JSON files recording every projection so it can be reversed.

### The two layers

| Layer | Lives at | Owned by | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| Global | `~/.mfaw/` | User (per machine) | Default skill set for all projects |
| Project | `<repo>/.mfaw/` | Project (committed to git) | Pins, additions, exclusions for this repo only |

`global ⊕ project` = **effective set** = what gets projected to `~/.claude/`.

