## 4. Data Model

### Asset

The atomic unit. Every skill / agent / rule / command is an "asset."

```python
@dataclass(frozen=True)
class Asset:
    id: str                    # globally unique slug, kebab-case
    kind: AssetKind            # SKILL | AGENT | RULE | COMMAND
    version: str               # semver
    path: Path                 # absolute path to source folder/file
    owners: list[str]          # from OWNERS file or frontmatter
    adapters: list[str]        # which adapters this asset targets
    metadata: dict             # parsed frontmatter

class AssetKind(StrEnum):
    SKILL = "skill"
    AGENT = "agent"
    RULE = "rule"
    COMMAND = "command"
```

### EffectiveSet

The resolved set after `global ⊕ project`.

```python
@dataclass
class EffectiveSet:
    assets: dict[str, Asset]   # id -> Asset
    layer_origin: dict[str, Layer]  # id -> "global" | "project"
    pins: dict[str, str]       # id -> pinned version
    excluded: set[str]         # ids excluded by project
```

### Projection

The act of installing one Asset into one adapter. Recorded in the ledger.

```python
@dataclass
class Projection:
    asset_id: str
    asset_version: str
    adapter: str
    stub_kind: StubKind        # SYMLINK | JUNCTION | COPY
    source: Path
    target: Path
    sentinel_hash: str | None  # for COPY only
    installed_at: datetime
    layer: Layer               # "global" | "project"
```

