## 5. Core Concepts

### 5.1 Asset Frontmatter

Every `SKILL.md` / agent / command / rule starts with YAML frontmatter:

```markdown
---
id: imwg-fix-cve
name: Fix CVE
description: One-line user-visible summary
version: 1.4.2
kind: skill
owners: ["@security-team"]
adapters: ["claude", "cursor"]
trigger: when the user asks to remediate a CVE
references:
  - references/cve-patterns.md
---

# Body — instructions Claude/Cursor reads
```

Validated against `schema/skill.schema.json` on every install, sync, and publish.

### 5.2 OWNERS file

Optional `OWNERS` file in any asset directory:

```
@security-team
@platform-infra
```

Used by `mfaw publish` to set PR reviewers. If absent, fall back to
`metadata.owners` in frontmatter.

### 5.3 Sentinel (for copy-fallback stubs)

When mfaw must copy a file (Windows non-admin, single file), it writes a
sentinel comment so `nuke` knows it's mfaw-managed:

```markdown
<!-- mfaw:managed asset=imwg-fix-cve version=1.4.2 sha=abc123… -->
---
name: ...
---
```

`nuke` removes only files whose first line matches `<!-- mfaw:managed`.

### 5.4 Settings.json hook tagging

When mfaw merges hook entries into `~/.claude/settings.json`, it tags them:

```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      {
        "_mfaw_managed": "asset:imwg-fix-cve@1.4.2",
        "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "node …" }]
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

`nuke` removes only entries with the `_mfaw_managed` field.

