## 10. Per-Repo Registry Layer

### `<repo>/.mfaw/manifest.json`

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://schemas.mfaw.dev/project-manifest-v1.json",
  "version": 1,
  "extends": "global",
  "pin": {
    "fix-cve": "1.4.2"
  },
  "add": [
    {
      "id": "proj-deploy-checks",
      "type": "skill",
      "path": ".mfaw/content/skills/proj-deploy-checks"
    }
  ],
  "exclude": ["legacy-style"],
  "adapters": {
    "claude": { "enabled": true },
    "cursor": { "enabled": false }
  },
  "metadata": {
    "owners": ["@team-platform"],
    "description": "Billing service skills"
  }
}
```

### Resolution rules (deterministic)

```python
def resolve(global_manifest, project_manifest, adapters) -> EffectiveSet:
    eff = EffectiveSet()

    # 1. Start with global, filtered by enabled adapters
    enabled = enabled_adapters(project_manifest, adapters)
    for asset in global_manifest.assets:
        if any(a in asset.adapters for a in enabled):
            eff.add(asset, layer=GLOBAL)

    if not project_manifest:
        return eff

    # 2. Apply pins
    for id, version in project_manifest.pin.items():
        if id not in eff.assets:
            raise UnknownAsset(id)
        eff.assets[id] = global_manifest.get_version(id, version)
        eff.pins[id] = version

    # 3. Apply adds (project wins on collision)
    for entry in project_manifest.add:
        asset = load_asset(entry.path, entry.type)
        if entry.id in eff.assets:
            warn(f"Project asset {entry.id} shadows global")
        eff.add(asset, layer=PROJECT)

    # 4. Apply excludes
    for id in project_manifest.exclude:
        eff.assets.pop(id, None)
        eff.excluded.add(id)

    return eff
```

### `init --local` flow

1. Verify in git repo (`.git` exists).
2. Refuse if `.mfaw/` already present.
3. Create:
   ```
   .mfaw/
     manifest.json     # starter: extends=global, no pins/adds/excludes
     state.json        # empty
     content/{skills,agents,rules,commands}/.gitkeep
     README.md         # "this folder is managed by mfaw — see https://..."
   ```
4. Append to `.gitignore`:
   ```
   .mfaw/state.json
   ```
5. Install git hooks (§11).
6. Register in `~/.mfaw/projects/index.json`:
   ```json
   { "<sha256(absolute_path)>": { "path": "...", "registered_at": "..." } }
   ```
7. Run `mfaw sync`.

### Switching projects

v1: single active project.

```python
# ~/.mfaw/config.toml
[active]
project = "/Users/x/code/billing"
```

`sync` always uses `cwd`'s nearest `.mfaw/` first, falling back to `active.project`.

