## 12. Publish Workflow

### Goal

Author edits → schema-checked, semver-bumped, ownership-routed PR.

### `mfaw publish` flow

```
1. AUTHOR phase
   User has edited content/skills/<id>/SKILL.md (or any asset).

2. DETECT phase
   git diff --name-only against origin/main → changed asset paths.
   For each, parse old (git show :origin/main:path) and new frontmatter.

3. CLASSIFY phase
   Diff frontmatter:
     - Body changed only           → patch bump
     - Optional field added        → minor bump
     - Required field removed      → major bump
     - Trigger / contract changed  → major bump
   Suggest version. Compare to user-set version. Error if mismatch.

4. VALIDATE phase (gates)
   ✓ schema valid (against skill.schema.json)
   ✓ all references/* paths resolve
   ✓ no secrets (regex sweep — AWS keys, GH tokens, etc.)
   ✓ frontmatter version matches semver bump rule
   ✓ owners list non-empty (OWNERS file or frontmatter)
   ✓ at least one example block in body OR a references/example.md
   ✓ trigger sentence < 200 chars
   Each gate prints PASS or FAIL. Any FAIL aborts unless --force.

5. PROPOSE phase
   Auto-generate PR body:
     ## What
     <auto-generated from diff>
     ## Why
     <user-provided one-liner from --message or interactive prompt>
     ## Affected adapters
     <from manifest>
     ## Reviewers
     <OWNERS or frontmatter.owners>
     ## Quality gates
     ✓ schema  ✓ refs  ✓ secrets  ✓ semver  ✓ owners
     ## Version
     <old> → <new> (<patch|minor|major>)

6. SHIP phase
   Branch:  <git user>/publish-<asset-id>-<new-version>
   Commit:  conventional: skill(<id>): bump to <version> — <one-liner>
   Push:    git push -u origin <branch>
   PR:      gh pr create --base main --title <title> --body <body>
            [--draft if --draft]
            --reviewer <owners>

7. RECORD phase
   ~/.mfaw/state.json:
     pending_publications.append({
       asset_id, version, branch, pr_url, sha, opened_at
     })
```

### `mfaw publish --status`

Lists pending publications with PR state (open/merged/closed) via `gh pr view`.

### `mfaw pull` warns on pending edits

If `git status --porcelain content/` shows un-published changes, `pull`
warns and refuses unless `--force`. Prevents accidental clobber.

